# Whole-board configuration transaction.
#
# The firmware only applies configuration through one CONFIG command that
# validates the ENTIRE staged area, and CONFIG writes flash. Therefore this
# service is a transaction, never a per-cycle write: the driver stages every
# channel, compares the staged area against what was requested, sends CONFIG
# once, then reads the effective values back and reports them.
#
# channels EMPTY means "keep what the board has": the driver reads the currently
# APPLIED configuration of all four channels and re-stages those exact values. It does
# NOT fall back to the YAML file -- silently replacing a board's stored role, gear or
# rpm with a file default is how a working arm gets mis-configured.
#
# A partial list changes only the listed channels; every other channel keeps its
# current board value. If the resulting staged area is identical to what the board
# already has, CONFIG is NOT sent at all (no pointless flash write) and `changed`
# comes back false.
#
# commit=false stages and reads back WITHOUT sending CONFIG, so an operator can
# inspect the staged area before committing.
ChannelConfig[] channels
bool commit
---
bool accepted
bool changed               # false when nothing differed, so CONFIG was not sent
uint16 sequence
uint16 result_code
bool persisted             # dirty, storage_error and pending_save all zero after commit
ChannelConfig[] staged     # staged area as read back (base+8..12 per channel)
ChannelConfig[] applied    # effective configuration as read back (base+0..4 per channel)
string message
